-- ── story 2-3a: the gate-in (an inbound vehicle visit) and the receipt link ──
-- Generated by drizzle-kit (the two tables, `goods_receipt_notes.gate_in_id`
-- and the four indexes) and hand-amended below the generated part: the
-- fail-fast guard, every CHECK, RLS (the tenant arm — neither table carries a
-- client: a truck can carry several clients' goods, decision 1) and the
-- post-migration probe (drizzle-kit is blind to all of it; `bun run
-- db:generate` afterwards reports "No schema changes").
--
-- Additive: two new tenant-scoped tables, empty at deploy, and one nullable
-- column on `goods_receipt_notes` (no default, no rewrite — every existing
-- receipt stays unlinked, which is what a receipt without a gate-in means,
-- decision 5). No data is rewritten. No foreign keys (IMPLEMENTATION-GUIDE §3).
--
-- Deliberately NO time-ordering CHECK (unload start ≥ gated in, end ≥ start,
-- gated out ≥ gated in): the handheld's times are taken as sent (a device
-- clock may be behind the gate desk's), so only the web commands order them.
--
-- Lock cost: the ADD COLUMN takes a brief ACCESS EXCLUSIVE lock on
-- `goods_receipt_notes` (no rewrite — nullable, no default); its index is
-- built non-concurrently (the 0081 precedent — concurrent index builds are
-- roadmap 6.2).

-- ── 0. fail-fast ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
DO $$
BEGIN
	IF EXISTS (
		SELECT 1 FROM information_schema.tables
		 WHERE table_schema = 'public' AND table_name = 'gate_ins'
	) THEN
		RAISE EXCEPTION 'migration 0086: the gate_ins table already exists — this migration has already been applied.';
	END IF;
END $$;
